# Cr2O3 (R-3c, rhombohedral primitive cell with the hexagonal c axis along z;
# generated with pymatgen from a = 4.9587, c = 13.5942 A, Cr 12c z = 0.3475,
# O 18e x = 0.3057). Ordered by height along c the Cr sites are Cr3, Cr2,
# Cr4, Cr1: GM1- z is the Cr2O3 order (+ - + -, R-3'c', magnetoelectric),
# GM1+ z the hematite order below the Morin transition (+ - - +, R-3c).
# The in-plane orders belong to GM3+ and GM3- (two copies each of a 2-dim
# irrep): the partners lie along the two-fold axis x (the a axis) and along
# y, the same for every copy; the GM3+ octupole is the in-plane hematite
# order, the GM3- copies the in-plane orders + - + - and + + - -, all with
# monoclinic groups
crystod-mag -c 167_PPOSCAR_Cr2O3 --element Cr --qpoint GM --classify-only

* Structure *
  Space group: R-3c (#167)
  Magnetic sites: Cr x 4
    Cr1: [0.8475, 0.8475, 0.8475]
    Cr2: [0.3475, 0.3475, 0.3475]
    Cr3: [0.1525, 0.1525, 0.1525]
    Cr4: [0.6525, 0.6525, 0.6525]

* Selected Q point *
  Selected q-point: GAMMA = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]

* Spin (axial-vector) representation *
  Spin (axial-vector) representation on Cr sites: 12 dimensions
  Decomposition: GM1+(1) + GM1-(1) + GM2+(1) + GM2-(1) + 2 x GM3+(2) + 2 x GM3-(2)

* Symmetry-adapted spin bases *
  GM1+(1): dim 1 [AFM, octupole]
  GM1-(1): dim 1 [AFM, quadrupole]
  GM2+(1): dim 1 [FM, dipole]
  GM2-(1): dim 1 [AFM, hexadecapole]
  GM3+(2): dim 2 [FM, dipole]
  GM3+(2): dim 2 [AFM, octupole]
  GM3-(2): dim 2 [AFM, quadrupole]
  GM3-(2): dim 2 [AFM, quadrupole]

* Magnetic groups and collinear classes *
basis                        component  MSG (BNS)         type  MPG    net magnetization  class
GM1+(1) [AFM, octupole]      z          R-3c (167.103)    I     -3m    none               altermagnet (g-wave)
GM1-(1) [AFM, quadrupole]    z          R-3'c' (167.106)  III   -3'm'  none               antiferromagnet (P T)
GM2+(1) [FM, dipole]         z          R-3c' (167.107)   III   -3m'   along z            ferromagnet
GM2-(1) [AFM, hexadecapole]  z          R-3'c (167.105)   III   -3'm   none               antiferromagnet (P T)
GM3+(2) [FM, dipole]         x          C2/c (15.85)      I     2/m    along x            ferromagnet
GM3+(2) [FM, dipole]         y          C2'/c' (15.89)    III   2'/m'  in the yz plane    ferromagnet
GM3+(2) [AFM, octupole]      y          C2/c (15.85)      I     2/m    along x            altermagnet (g-wave)
GM3+(2) [AFM, octupole]      x          C2'/c' (15.89)    III   2'/m'  in the yz plane    altermagnet (g-wave)
GM3-(2) [AFM, quadrupole]    x          C2'/c (15.87)     III   2'/m   none               antiferromagnet (P T)
GM3-(2) [AFM, quadrupole]    y          C2/c' (15.88)     III   2/m'   none               antiferromagnet (P T)
GM3-(2) [AFM, quadrupole]    y_2        C2'/c (15.87)     III   2'/m   none               antiferromagnet (P T)
GM3-(2) [AFM, quadrupole]    x_2        C2/c' (15.88)     III   2/m'   none               antiferromagnet (P T)

MSG: magnetic space group from the moment directions (BNS number, type I-IV);
MPG: magnetic point group; net magnetization: the direction allowed by symmetry;
class: from the signs of the moments along their common axis only (nonrelativistic).
MSG and MPG symbols are in the standard BNS setting; directions are in the Cartesian axes of the input cell.

All AFM bases satisfy sum_i S_i = 0; FM entries carry the cluster dipole moment.
Reference: M.-T. Suzuki et al., PRB 95, 094406 (2017); PRB 99, 174407 (2019).
Reference (collinear classes): L. Smejkal, J. Sinova and T. Jungwirth, Phys. Rev. X 12, 031042 (2022).


