# P4/m Ti2Ga3 (Ti 4k): GM3+ and GM4+ (and GM3-, GM4-) are one-dimensional complex
# irreps; each conjugate pair is one real two-dimensional space, listed under
# its pair label GM3+GM4+(2) with the FM dipole (moments along x and y) and the
# in-plane octupole (a d-wave altermagnet) separated
crystod-mag -c ../test_POSCARs/83_PPOSCAR_Ti2Ga3 --element Ti --qpoint GM --classify-only

* Structure *
  Space group: P4/m (#83)
  Magnetic sites: Ti x 4
    Ti1: [0.873483, 0.69647, 0.5]
    Ti2: [0.69647, 0.126517, 0.5]
    Ti3: [0.30353, 0.873483, 0.5]
    Ti4: [0.126517, 0.30353, 0.5]

* Selected Q point *
  Selected q-point: GAMMA = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]

* Spin (axial-vector) representation *
  Spin (axial-vector) representation on Ti sites: 12 dimensions
  Decomposition: GM1+(1) + 2 x GM1-(1) + 2 x GM3+GM4+(2) + GM3-GM4-(2) + GM2+(1) + 2 x GM2-(1)

* Symmetry-adapted spin bases *
  GM1+(1): dim 1 [FM, dipole]
  GM1-(1): dim 1 [AFM, quadrupole]
  GM1-(1): dim 1 [AFM, hexadecapole]
  GM3+GM4+(2): dim 2 [FM, dipole]
  GM3+GM4+(2): dim 2 [AFM, octupole]
  GM3-GM4-(2): dim 2 [AFM, quadrupole]
  GM2+(1): dim 1 [AFM, octupole]
  GM2-(1): dim 1 [AFM, quadrupole]
  GM2-(1): dim 1 [AFM, quadrupole]

* Magnetic groups and collinear classes *
basis                          component  MSG (BNS)       type  MPG    net magnetization  class
